issues.body:
### 🐛 Describe the bug

To track CMPLRLLVM-78818

nextafter(-denorm_min, +1) steps from the smallest negative subnormal toward a larger value; the next representable number is zero. Per IEEE-754 the sign of a zero result follows the first argument, so it must be -0.0  (signbit = 1). On device, sycl::nextafter (and std::nextafter) returns +0.0 (signbit = 0) instead, for both float and double.

reproducer:

#include <sycl/sycl.hpp>#include <cmath>
#include <cstdio>
#include <limits>template <typename T>
void run(sycl::queue& q, const char* name) {
  const T from = -std::numeric_limits<T>::denorm_min();
  T* r = sycl::malloc_shared<T>(1, q);
  q.single_task([=]() { r[0] = sycl::nextafter(from, T(1)); }).wait();
  printf("%-7s signbit=%d  %s\n", name, std::signbit(r[0]) ? 1 : 0,
         std::signbit(r[0]) ? "OK (-0.0)" : "WRONG (+0.0)");
  sycl::free(r, q);
}int main() {
  sycl::queue q{sycl::gpu_selector_v};
  printf("Device: %s\n",
         q.get_device().get_info<sycl::info::device::name>().c_str());
  run<float>(q, "float");
  run<double>(q, "double");
  return 0;
}


### Versions

2026.1

