Nightly wheel torch 2.16.0.dev20261019+xpu on BMG (Intel(R) Arc(TM) Pro B60 Graphics, runner xpu-agent). The issue's reproducer was run as a script with a CPU-division oracle, from outside any pytorch checkout.



Test case
Verdict
Observed




div(xpu_tensor, python_scalar) over 27 (dtype, scalar, rounding_mode) combos
REPRODUCED
summary: signature=27 other=0 total=27 -- XPU inf (fp16 nan) where CPU is finite



All 27 combinations of {float32, bfloat16, float16} x {1e-39, 5e-40, 1e-45} x {None, "trunc", "floor"} show the signature; other=0 confirms the oracle is not flagging ordinary rounding noise. Example rows:
