Summary
Outcome: IMPLEMENTING(fix_verified)
One bug behind all 27 reported combinations: the CPU-scalar fast path in the XPU true/trunc/floor division kernels multiplied by a host-computed 1 / b without ever checking that the reciprocal survived, so for b around 1e-39 it overflowed to inf in float and mapped every finite element to +-inf (and 0 to NaN). The fix adds a host-side is_usable_reciprocal guard in BinaryInternal.h and, when it rejects the reciprocal, dispatches a fallback that really divides in the accumulate type; the fast path is untouched and bit-identical. Verification was a genuine A/B on a single source build -- signature=0 with the fix, signature=27 with only these four files reverted and rebuilt -- plus 1555 and 397 passing div-family cases in test_binary_ufuncs.py and test_ops.py, and clean lint.
