One thing for the reviewer to decide, not a defect in the patch: CUDA carries the same unguarded reciprocal today, and the upstream attempt to fix it (pytorch/pytorch#201302) was closed unmerged by its own author within hours, with no review. So this patch makes XPU match CPU and diverge from CUDA. The earlier upstream not planned ruling on pytorch/pytorch#191495 was explicitly about the reciprocal path's one-bit divergence being acceptable, which does not cover inf/NaN for a finite quotient -- but whether XPU should lead CUDA here is a maintainer call.


